# Refusal tokens of ivs_asm (plan 07-04, T5, D-17): one token per line, the exact set the tool can print.
# A refusal is one stderr line `ivs_asm: <token>: <source>:<line>: <detail>`, exit status 1, no output file.
# The suite asm (tests/asm-tap.sh) pins this list three ways: every token has exactly one case
# asm.neg.<token> (a source tests/asm/neg/<token>.asm, or one built at run time for asm-syntax, a CR line
# end, and asm-limit, a line above 255 bytes); every token the source tools/asm/asm.c can print is in this
# list; and every file in tests/asm/neg names a token of this list. Adjust it only with a reason in the
# summary of the plan that changes it.
asm-syntax
asm-mnemonic
asm-operand-count
asm-operand-kind
asm-register
asm-symbol-undefined
asm-symbol-duplicate
asm-symbol-reserved
asm-expr
asm-imm-range
asm-imm-sdbd
asm-sdbd-target
asm-direct-range
asm-branch-range
asm-decle-range
asm-org
asm-window
asm-spelling
asm-header
asm-limit
